<h2 id="ha-ctrl-005-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Check Heat/Idle, Heat/Heating, Off, unknown and unavailable independently. A mode change must not falsely update measured temperature.
2. Exercise decimal steps, Celsius and Fahrenheit, single and dual targets, invalid ordering and a mode removed while editing.
3. Test a fan without oscillation, a dehumidifier with no current humidity and a water heater without a reported temperature. No invented controls or zeroes.
4. Reject a target request and delay another beyond the waiting limit. Preserve native safety/code flows, keyboard access, source precision and meaningful pending text.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

